## Assessment Structure

Units 1, 2, 4 and 5 may include:
- Multiple-choice questions.
- Short-answer questions.
- Open-response questions.
- Calculations.
- Extended-writing questions.

Units 3 and 6 assess practical and experimental skills.

Unit 5 includes questions based on a pre-released
scientific article.

## Mathematical Assessment

Minimum Level 2 mathematics marks:

- Unit 1: 8 marks.
- Unit 2: 8 marks.
- Unit 3: 5 marks.
- Unit 4: 9 marks.
- Unit 5: 9 marks.
- Unit 6: 5 marks.

At least 10% of marks across the qualification assess
mathematical skills at Level 2 or above.

