# 2. Assessment Objectives

## AO1 — Knowledge and Understanding

Demonstrate accurate knowledge and understanding of biology.

Includes:
- Scientific terminology.
- Biological structures.
- Mechanisms.
- Processes.
- Principles.

Overall IAL weighting: 34–37%.

## AO2a — Application

Apply biological knowledge to familiar and unfamiliar contexts.

Includes:
- Applying mechanisms to new situations.
- Interpreting biological processes.
- Using knowledge to explain observations.

Overall IAL weighting: 33–36%.

## AO2b — Analysis and Evaluation

Analyse and evaluate scientific information.

Includes:
- Interpreting evidence.
- Making judgements.
- Drawing conclusions.
- Evaluating biological explanations.

Overall IAL weighting: 11–14%.

## AO3 — Experimental Skills

Demonstrate experimental knowledge and skills.

Includes:
- Experimental design.
- Data interpretation.
- Evaluation of methods.
- Uncertainty and errors.
- Practical techniques.

Overall IAL weighting: 17–18%.

These objectives operate together.
Individual questions may assess more than one objective.

