# 9. Mathematical Skills

## Percentages

Percentage change =
(final - initial) / initial × 100

Percentage uncertainty =
absolute uncertainty / measured value × 100

## Rates

Rate = change in quantity / time

## Magnification

Magnification = image size / actual size

## Surface Area

Sphere:
A = 4πr²

Circle:
A = πr²

## Volume

Sphere:
V = 4/3 πr³

## Cardiac Output

Cardiac output =
heart rate × stroke volume

## Respiratory Quotient

RQ = carbon dioxide produced / oxygen consumed

## Population Genetics

Hardy-Weinberg:
p + q = 1

p² + 2pq + q² = 1

## Ecology

Index of diversity:

D = N(N - 1) / Σ[n(n - 1)]

N = total number of organisms.
n = number of organisms of each species.

## Statistical Interpretation

Students should understand:
- Mean.
- Median.
- Mode.
- Range.
- Standard deviation.
- Correlation.
- Statistical significance.
- Null hypotheses.

Select statistical tests appropriate to the question
and any instructions or formulae provided.

