# 10. Examination Command Words

## State

Give a concise fact.

## Give / Name

Provide the requested term or example.

## Describe

Identify characteristics, observations or patterns.

## Explain

Use relevant scientific reasons and mechanisms.

## Compare

Identify relevant similarities and differences.

## Calculate

Show working and provide an appropriate final value.

## Determine

Use the supplied information to establish an answer.

## Suggest

Apply knowledge to an unfamiliar context.

## Discuss

Consider different relevant aspects with supporting reasoning.

## Evaluate

Assess evidence, advantages, limitations and implications.

Use the actual question and mark scheme to determine
the required breadth and depth.

